# Folder document models for writers

## Product audience
Futura Nota serves novelists, storytellers, and teams using storytelling for a business. Folder document presentation should support both narrative browsing and compact contextual links.

## Two presentation models
| Model | Creation path | Folder body presentation | Open action |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Descriptive** | Left panel → **Create a new Document** | Title + `Description: {excerpt}` + `continue reading`; no color handle | `continue reading` |
| **Color link** | Inside open folder → **Create a document** | Title + color-link handle only; no Description or `continue reading` | Color handle |

Do not expose two open actions on the color-link model. Folder `viewMode` (`story` | `quick`) now drives open-folder presentation for all linked docs; keep `hideColorLink` as the fallback discriminator when `folderViewMode` is not passed.

## Source of truth
- Descriptive creation sets `parentDocId`; `syncNodeToParentDoc` inserts/updates a linked H1/TODO with `hideColorLink: true`.
- Inside-folder creation keeps `hideColorLink: false` and the visible color handle.
- Open-folder rendering prefers folder `viewMode` over per-block `hideColorLink` (presentation only; do not rewrite blocks on switch).
- This must work for every folder document, not a one-off title.

## Where Description appears
| Surface | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Left panel folder expand | **Title only** (File icon + title) |
| Open folder body, descriptive model only | Under linked H1/TODO: `Description: {excerpt} continue reading` (+ status if set) |
| Open folder body, color-link model | Never show Description, `continue reading`, or its duplicate open route |

## Delete rules
1. **Delete from left panel expand** → purge node entity **and** title/Description/blocks from the parent folder (`deleteNode` → `deleteNodeAndDocBlocks`).
2. **Remove layers inside the open folder** (detach / empty-title delete) → strip the linked owner bundle from folder blocks, but **keep** the document under the folder in the left panel (`parentDocId` retained).

## Data
- Excerpt from `node.content` **body** via `getNodeWritingExcerpt` / `getNodeWritingBodyPlainText` (max 260)
- `continue reading` opens descriptive documents only
- `mergeMissingLinkedOwnerBundles` + draft purge when node deleted from panel

## Key files
- `LinkedMacronodeDescription.jsx` — Description line under linked titles
- `DocBlockStack.jsx` — mounts Description; respects `hideColorLink`
- `nodesStore.syncNodeToParentDoc` + `panelSyncedBlockFields`
- `docNodeSync.removeLinkedOwnerBundleFromBlocks` / `mergeMissingLinkedOwnerBundles`
